---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Typography Reference"
  description="Typography elements and styles used on this site"
>
  <h1>Typography Reference</h1>
  <p>
    This page documents all typography elements and styling available on this
    site.
  </p>

  <h2>Headings</h2>
  <p>The site uses a monospace font for all headings with varying sizes:</p>
  <h1>Heading 1 (h1) - 4xl, bold</h1>
  <h2>Heading 2 (h2) - 2xl, bold with border</h2>
  <h3>Heading 3 (h3) - xl, bold</h3>
  <h4>Heading 4 (h4) - bold</h4>
  <h5>Heading 5 (h5) - bold</h5>
  <h6>Heading 6 (h6) - bold</h6>

  <h2>Paragraphs</h2>
  <p>
    Regular paragraph text with relaxed line height and bottom margin spacing.
  </p>
  <p>This is another paragraph to show spacing between paragraphs.</p>

  <h2>Links</h2>
  <p>
    Links are styled in <a href="#">blue with hover underline</a> in light mode and
    <a href="#">light blue in dark mode</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Unordered Lists</h2>
  <p>Unordered lists use disc bullets:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>First item</li>
    <li>Second item</li>
    <li>
      Third item with nested list:
      <ul>
        <li>Nested item 1</li>
        <li>Nested item 2</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Ordered Lists</h2>
  <p>Ordered lists use decimal numbering:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>First step</li>
    <li>Second step</li>
    <li>
      Third step with nested list:
      <ol>
        <li>Nested step 1</li>
        <li>Nested step 2</li>
      </ol>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Inline Code</h2>
  <p>
    Inline code appears like this: <code>const variable = "example";</code> with a
    subtle background and padding.
  </p>

  <h2>Code Blocks</h2>
  <p>Code blocks have a full background with borders:</p>
  <pre><code>function example() {
  `return true;`
}</code></pre>

  <h2>Tables</h2>
  <p>Tables use monospace font with alternating row colors:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Header 1</th>
        <th>Header 2</th>
        <th>Header 3</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Cell 1</td>
        <td>Cell 2</td>
        <td>Cell 3</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Cell 4</td>
        <td>Cell 5</td>
        <td>Cell 6</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Callout Blocks</h2>
  <p>
    Callout blocks highlight important information with colored left borders:
  </p>

  <div class="callout note">
    <strong>Note:</strong> This is a standard note callout with a blue border.
  </div>

  <div class="callout tip">
    <strong>Tip:</strong> This is a tip callout with a green border.
  </div>

  <div class="callout warning">
    <strong>Warning:</strong> This is a warning callout with a yellow border.
  </div>

  <h2>Badges</h2>
  <p>Badges for tagging and categorization:</p>
  <p>
    <span class="badge">Tag 1</span>
    <span class="badge">Tag 2</span>
    <span class="badge">Tag 3</span>
  </p>

  <h2>Step Blocks</h2>
  <p>Step blocks for multi-step processes:</p>
  <div class="step">
    <span class="step-number">Step 1</span>
    <p>First step of the process</p>
  </div>
  <div class="step">
    <span class="step-number">Step 2</span>
    <p>Second step of the process</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Color Palette</h2>
  <div class="landing-grid">
    <div class="landing-card">
      <h3 style="color: rgb(37, 99, 235);">Primary Blue</h3>
      <p>Used for headings, links, and primary UI elements</p>
      <code style="background: #dbeafe;">#2563eb</code>
    </div>
    <div class="landing-card">
      <h3 style="color: rgb(22, 163, 74);">Success Green</h3>
      <p>Used for positive actions and success states</p>
      <code style="background: #dcfce7;">#16a34a</code>
    </div>
    <div class="landing-card">
      <h3 style="color: rgb(234, 179, 8);">Warning Yellow</h3>
      <p>Used for warnings and alerts</p>
      <code style="background: #fef3c7;">#eab308</code>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
